# PlayerSelect_Run ($0656B0): paths the corpus never takes. The select loop only ends through
# g_SceneExitTimer ($FFCC66), so each case presets it to 2: two frames run and the screen ends
# (no input needed). Each frame waits for V-blank by polling the VDP status (VBLANK bit 3
# clear, then set): the hardware reads alternate $0000 / $0008, far more than needed.
# Not reachable here: two-player stepping's wait for the frame tick ($065BD2-$065BDC, $065BF8:
# g_FrameTick is set only by the V-int, and synthetic runs take no interrupts) and a player who
# joins on this screen getting health $700 ($065C2A: needs pad input over several frames).
case magneto_six
# both players were Magneto before his stage: each gets a random other character
w $FFCC64 = 0
b $FFC644 = 6
